pologicalSpace.{u} X] →\n    {motive : RegularSpace.{u} X → Sort u_1} →\n      (t : RegularSpace.{u} X) →\n        ((regular : ∀ {s : Set.{u} X} {a : X}, IsClosed.{u} s → a ∉ s → Disjoint.{u} (nhdsSet.{u} s) (nhds.{u} a)) →\n            motive ⋯) →\n          motive t","unsafe":false,"value":136,"source":{"code":"/-- A topological space is called a *regular space* if for any closed set `s` and `a ∉ s`, there\nexist disjoint open sets `U ⊇ s` and `V ∋ a`. We formulate this condition in terms of `Disjoint`ness\nof filters `𝓝ˢ s` and `𝓝 a`. -/\n@[mk_iff]\nclass RegularSpace (X : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] : Prop where\n  /-- If `a` is a point that does not belong to a closed set `s`, then `a` and `s` admit disjoint\n  neighborhoods. -/\n  regular : ∀ {s : Set X} {a}, IsClosed s → a ∉ s → Disjoint (𝓝ˢ s) (𝓝 a)","start":75,"end":82},"axioms":["Quot.sound","propext"]}